From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan WEGENER <steph.wegener@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:09:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] [Onyx] The compositor on the V3D, stage 2: layers for
 animated opacity / transform, animations by the compositor, scrolling without
 layouts

Layers for CSS animations and transitions of opacity and transform (the Animation and
AnimatedOpacity triggers): GraphicsLayerOnyx takes them (addAnimation, evaluated at composite
time with TextureMapperAnimation, which is GL-free: its guards widened), so an animated frame
paints nothing and needs no page update. A layer drawn scaled, rotated or at a fractional place
is one bilinear texture when it fits 2048; opacity over overlapping composited descendants goes
through a group (a gpucomp alpha target, uploaded again as a texture). A budget of textures and
pixels (440, 96 MB). A dirty tile is repainted only where it is dirty (up to 8 rectangles a
layer).

Scrolling: a page's sticky elements are layers when the frame is composited
(RenderLayerCompositor), and a composited fixed or sticky element is not laid out again when the
layout viewport moves (LocalFrameView: its layer's place is updated instead) -- a scroll step
laid out every such element and repainted its block. RenderLayer::paintList skips a child
subtree none of whose repaint rectangles touches what is painted, when a composited layer's
content is painted (a small repaint walked every layer of the page).

Switches (files in SD:/etc): web-gpu-debug, web-gpu-trace, web-gpu-3d, web-gpu-noanim,
web-gpu-nogroups, web-gpu-nocull, web-gpu-stage1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
